  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "comment": "Reviewed consumer environments: the exact Solid 2 trees real consumers install. `bun scripts/ecosystem-benchmark/run.mjs --consumer-environment <id>` certifies each listed package, cloned from its solid2 manifest row, in that tree, as a delivery-only run: it may feed the compiled-in tier (`make consumer-environment-runs`, then `make accepted-bundles`) and the coverage census refuses it. Its yield is measured by re-sweeping the consumer named in `source`, never by the census pin. Derive an entry with `derive-consumer-environment.mjs` and review it; run.mjs refuses any package whose version or integrity differs from its manifest row, and any runtime that is not an audited archive or is above AUDITED_SOLID_2 (lib/families.mjs). `unmatched` lists the closure packages that are not certified here, and why.",
